WEBVTT

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.860
I decided to write a story, to cure my boredom.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.900
But my brush won't move at all.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.660
Then you should try to 
conquer the land, Onee-sama.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.030
That would be much more entertaining.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.690
But I'm not interested in conquest.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.460
Conquest...

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.680
Not interested.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.900
I'll leave that to Nobunaga-dono.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.080
Then let's send something to Nobunaga-san.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.560
Send something?

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.190
I just got a splendid hunting hawk...

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.860
I'm sure Nobunaga-dono would love it.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.950
We could have her join us for a hunt...

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.600
I can't wait!

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:01.680
I'm really looking forward to it, too.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.000
<i>In many ways.</i>

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:39.010
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:39.010
<b>Ghost Story Girl</b>

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.260
What's hawk-hunting?

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.610
It means using a trained hawk to hunt.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.890
It's a primary form of 
entertainment around here.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:54.070
Your lord is quite a fan of hawks, as well.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:58.030
Lords from other countries 
come and bring her hawks.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.380
Does hunting mean I get meat, for once?

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.770
A banquet! A banquet!

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.700
A banquet with meat from hunted beasts!

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.350
I'll come, too!

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.840
Shingen-san... And Kenshin-san, also.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.140
Quite a splendid hawk!

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.090
Well done, Ieyasu.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.930
No, not at all...

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.630
We didn't even invite you guys...

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:29.210
You're not here to regain your armor, are you?

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.640
Of course not.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:32.900
I received a letter

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.670
that a splendid banquet would be hosted here.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.440
What?

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.340
I'm sorry.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:42.250
I sent them both a letter...

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.710
We were all to go hawk hunting,

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.630
and then we'd have a banquet.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:50.450
I thought it would please you...

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:54.160
Ieyasu, you're a splendid girl.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.960
Would you like to be my retainer?

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.340
No, I want to take care of her!

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.240
Wait! I want to...

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.780
What are you talking about?

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.470
Ieyasu-chan is practically my sister!

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.450
No, me!

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:06.110
Me!

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.470
Me!

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.720
Then me, too...

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:12.330
You're a dog. What do you want with her?

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.900
Well, maybe she could take care of me.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.790
So that's your type...

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:19.020
Don't be jealous.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.030
What? You think you're 
my boyfriend or something?

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.990
Everyone left already, by the way.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.280
Wait for me!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.750
I'm coming, too!

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.280
I want meat!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.500
Jeez...

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.760
I want meat, too...

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.840
Everyone has too much endurance...

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.150
Don't fall behind, Hideyoshi!

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.510
Don't you want to see my bird's heroics?

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:53.440
Your bird? Which bird?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.270
Tokunyan?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.700
Tokunyan!

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:04.370
I'm sorry, Hideyoshi-san.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.700
Is something wrong?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.120
Not at all.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.340
Let's get going.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.530
If we're late, Akerin will yell at us.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.830
<i>She's not...</i>

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.000
Go, go!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.380
What kind of bird is that?

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.030
A pheasant... I've never had one.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.930
Anyway, go!

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:36.870
The hawk Ieyasu gave you is well-trained.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.300
Nobunaga-san's just skilled with it.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.070
You flatter me.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.070
You guys can stop talking like 
a bunch of golfing businessmen.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:47.240
Let's go!

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.240
We can have pheasant!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.910
And duck soup!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.810
But duck noodles might also be good...

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:58.120
You're really hungry, aren't you?

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.500
I haven't had meat in forever!

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.030
A bunny?

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.510
I want to keep it!

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.130
Catch it!

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.570
It's not coming back.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.650
My lord, what will we do?

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.440
Hideyoshi, you want to keep that rabbit?

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.190
I do!

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:27.590
Very well!

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:29.700
Everyone, let's go!

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.890
It's nearly dark as night.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:45.460
This area is known as the Sea of Trees.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.500
It really is thick.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:50.100
Actually, in thick forests like this, 
don't you normally...

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.610
I can't see anything from up here, either.

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.800
Yoshimoto-san?

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.020
Don't scare us like that!

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.750
Hanging from a rope, in a forest...

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.840
I can see a light farther in.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.280
Someone might be there.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:17.260
It would be good to have some light.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.000
Let us go there...

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:24.670
This is a hill of the beheaded, then?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.550
The beheaded?

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:30.360
The heads of those 
beheaded during a war are buried here.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.970
Oh, so it's a grave.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:35.140
The light's getting closer.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.180
Indeed.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.020
Is someone there?

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:56.080
What is this?

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.100
A tea party here, in the middle of a forest?

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.150
That's what you notice first?

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:03.920
They're dead... They're definitely dead!

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.990
These must be the ghosts 
of the fallen Genji warriors.

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:09.390
You're Date Masamune-dono.

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.800
Are you a ghost now, too?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.330
No, I'm alive.

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:16.750
Is that an acquaintance of yours, Mitsuhide-san?

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:15.690
<i>This is...</i>

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.330
Well, yes...

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:23.230
You look like someone I know, kinda...

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.470
I suppose Date-sensei 
doesn't have boobs that big...

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:33.440
So what are you doing here?

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.650
I was trying to travel through this forest,

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:40.460
when I was forced to join them, for their tea...

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.730
If you wish not to join them, simply leave.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:44.710
It isn't that easy.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.620
It seems they're telling one hundred stories.

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:53.920
To leave, I must tell stories that satisfy them.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.250
That's really hard...

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:58.760
One person couldn't do all 
of the hundred alone!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:05.440
Everyone, please help me 
to complete the hundred stories!

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:09.990
Goodbye.

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.900
We're in the midst of hawk hunting.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.020
What?

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.330
Let's keep hunting!

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:19.960
First, we must find that hawk.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:22.690
How awful...

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.630
Why?

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.420
You should give up.

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:37.340
I just got the direction wrong.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.850
Why?!

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:44.130
Shingen, go that way!

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:45.530
We'll go this way.

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:46.480
Right.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:58.850
Then, this way!

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.070
What about this way?

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.770
I'm thirsty.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.270
They have some tea, if you want it.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:32.360
So we have to join the 
hundred stories, no matter what?

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.570
Um, we just happened along this way.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.990
Let us go!

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.200
Say something...

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.000
If they won't talk, then kill them!

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.490
It's useless to wave your blades at the dead.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:54.380
So what should we do?

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:59.360
We should tell stories, like they want.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.770
Ieyasu-chan is right.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.220
I guess so...

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.470
What?

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:08.890
I'd really rather not...

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:24.110
Ieyasu-dono is the one who said to do it.

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:28.210
Why doesn't she show us how.

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:29.500
Very well.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.250
Tokunyan looks really spooky.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:36.500
This story is called "Ohana-san of the Privy."

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:39.190
In an empty privy...

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:40.890
What's wrong?

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:42.590
Is something in your ears?

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:44.510
No.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.660
In an empty privy...

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:53.790
My throat's bothering me.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.910
Are you not good with these, maybe?

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:59.310
Th-That's not it at all.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:01.710
Then let's listen to her.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:03.660
I know.

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:05.510
In an empty privy,

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:07.660
if you knock three times...

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.210
Thump.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:12.210
Thump.

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:13.700
Thump.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.210
And then say,

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.340
"Are you there, Ohana-san?"

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:27.390
That's the story.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:30.890
One of the candles went out!

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.670
Now we can go back.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:35.700
Of course not.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.400
One hundred stories doesn't end

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:40.590
until all hundred stories have been told.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:43.600
There are ninety-two left.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:44.700
No way...

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.940
At night, when you're walking along a road,

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:51.200
from behind you comes...

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:55.840
In the ruins of a castle, burned during a war,

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.000
you can hear a lute...

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:02.340
If you look into the mirror, 
exactly at midnight...

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:04.750
My lord!

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:06.760
I'm not your lord!

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:10.510
I'm terribly sorry.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.710
Hanging from the ceiling,

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:17.270
in the room where the armor was kept,

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:18.190
was...

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:21.570
Tie her up!

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:31.400
One day, a sinister letter...

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.870
I mean, a scroll arrived.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.940
It had only a single character written on it.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.960
Each day, a different letter,

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.670
with a different character arrived...

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.800
All right. It's my turn now.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:52.310
A baby was abandoned 
before a samurai's manor.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.910
The lord of the manor decided to take the baby

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.420
and raise it as her own.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.310
And then something amazing happened... {K: Leave this line.}

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:01.750
What do you think?

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:02.910
Scary, huh?

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:04.690
Is that all?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.670
What do you mean, is that all?

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:09.240
What kind of amazing thing happened?

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.430
What kind?

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:15.970
Like if they all died mysteriously...

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:19.650
You have to tell us that part, or it isn't scary.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:22.620
Oh, yeah... They're all dead.

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:25.170
It happened hundreds of years ago!

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.300
This isn't working...

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.180
It's my turn last.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:38.230
I'll begin.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:43.690
This story is really scary... 
You don't want to hear it.

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:46.280
It's supposed to be scary.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.780
Just tell the story.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.840
Don't blame me if you regret it.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.030
All right.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:15:02.050
On the grounds of a certain temple, 
stands a strange cedar tree...

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:08.050
I-If you touch that tree...

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:10.720
Tie her up again!

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.500
Twenty-eight, twenty-nine, thirty...

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.990
We're hardly getting anywhere...

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:43.890
None of my lord's stories count,

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:45.920
and Akerin's over there freaking out.

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:47.680
What do we do?

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.320
I'm out of stories.

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:51.720
I still have some.

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:54.910
Tokunyan's our only hope.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:57.110
Don't forget me!

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:59.960
My lord, it's one thing 
to want to do a good job,

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.310
but without this, it's no good.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.070
Just leave it to me.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:06.990
How could I conquer, 
if I couldn't even do this?

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.730
Then that's good, I guess.

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:12.800
And then, they heard a sound in the night.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:16.010
And the picture...

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:20.160
And she never spoke to anyone again.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:24.960
And then she woke up, and it was all a dream!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:30.550
And it was the stupidest thing ever!

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.850
But that wasn't scary at all!

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.550
Maybe I'll just blow them out!

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:44.480
Nobunaga-san wants to 
conquer the land, but look at her.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.440
It won't be easy for her.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:51.370
Wow... She's cute but sharp-tongued.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:56.220
Then I shall simultaneously eliminate 
all the candles, with the scariest story ever.

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:58.410
You couldn't possibly...

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.940
Oh, I had a really good one that I forgot!

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:03.960
It was a horror story

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.420
for the cell phone, and it's really scary!

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.930
I'll tell it.

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:11.440
Hideyoshi, give it to me.

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:16.310
You said you'd help me conquer, right?

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:17.090
But...

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.550
Just tell me!

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.600
All right...

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.290
Listen carefully.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.740
OK... Yeah.

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:34.110
You aren't supposed to laugh there!

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:40.160
The story I'm about to tell

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:44.120
could happen to anyone, anywhere.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:48.130
She seems to have 
learned how to tell a story.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:52.460
I guess I get the credit for teaching her.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:56.250
<i>Actually, she looks really scary...</i>

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:57.890
And then!

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.500
Then...

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:05.230
You didn't forget, did you?

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.070
And then, there was

00:18:09.070 --> 00:18:12.270
a clanking from the vending machine 
in front of the convenience store.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:15.650
And then, there was a clanking from the vending 
machine in front of the convenience store.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.290
Convenience store?

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:18.550
Vending machine?

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:19.800
Oh, crap!

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.270
Oh, crap.

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:23.500
No, don't repeat that part.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.250
No, don't repeat...

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:33.040
<i>Huh? They look kind of scared.</i>

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:36.550
<i>OK! I'll go with this.</i>

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:39.760
And what came out of the vending machine

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.790
was what the girl was holding when...

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:48.520
This is a true story.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:52.570
Something terrifying will happen to anyone

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:58.490
who hears it, without repeating it 
to four others within four days.

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:00.680
It's over...

00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:09.290
The candles...

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:16.400
Nobunaga-dono...

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:22.760
We see that you are one truly worthy to rule.

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:24.720
They spoke.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.110
The dead samurai spoke...

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:30.260
Worthy to rule...

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.600
Impressive, Nobunaga-dono.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:43.510
You really did it.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:46.660
That was a truly scary story.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:50.210
It was nothing!

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:56.810
I think they were just scared 
of you, not the story...

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:00.510
Oh, right. We need to let Akerin go!

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:03.180
Hey, Akerin...

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:12.080
Me, too!

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:15.310
We're back.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:21.690
We found the hawk, 
and Mitsuhide's kunai got the rabbit.

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:23.650
Everything worked out.

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:27.810
Let's go back and have a banquet!

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:30.230
I'm pretty hungry, too.

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:31.800
So am I!

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:37.440
That was quite a splendid job.

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:42.400
Nobunaga will undoubtedly collect all 
of the armor, now that her ego's inflated.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:45.700
And it won't be long before I take it from her.

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:50.310
Anyway, those Genji samurai 
were pretty well done.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:53.800
No, that was not our doing.

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:55.060
What?

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:56.810
Then what did you do?

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:58.320
Nothing, really.

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:02.210
Useless idiot.

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:09.240
Tokunyan was different from her usual self.

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:12.580
Eat up, you guys!

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:25.390
Look what happened to the rabbit!

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:27.680
You said you wanted it.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:30.310
I didn't say I wanted to eat it!

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:32.010
Don't be like that.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:35.180
Rabbits are yummy.

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:37.280
I-I'm fine.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:38.200
OK...

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:40.190
Come on!

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.200
Well?

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:45.810
<i>Oda's child general is truly worthy to rule.</i>

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:49.070
<i>The true ancestors have said so.</i>

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:52.850
<i>Well, I guess that's interesting...</i>

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.960
<i>In many ways.</i>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:52.410
<b>Sengoku Otome Style Preview</b>

00:23:25.390 --> 00:23:28.420
Sensei, why suddenly call me to the teacher's office?

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:33.330
<b>Date-Sensei 
Hirata Yuka</b>

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:33.330
<b>Hideyoshino 
Hidaka Rina</b>

00:23:28.830 --> 00:23:30.110
I wanted to hear

00:23:30.110 --> 00:23:33.330
a romantic story from your youth.

00:23:33.630 --> 00:23:35.290
A romantic story from my youth...

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:39.180
<b></b>

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:39.400
Let me see...

00:23:39.400 --> 00:23:43.570
When I was in elementary school,

00:23:43.570 --> 00:23:46.020
I liked a boy named Take-chan...

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:48.400
<b></b>

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:46.690
Take-chan?

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:48.930
So Take-chan...

00:23:48.930 --> 00:23:51.040
Take-chan moved...

00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:51.700
He moved.

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:52.410
Yeah.

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.220
Watch next time, OK?

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.480
Preview

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.480
Memory Maiden
